{
  "rationale": "Model sensing and motion as separate plants, then use compact specifications to map clear sensing to forward-progress actions and obstacle sensing to one-shot recovery actions. The policy favors move_forward in clear space, uses random_walk only as a secondary clear-space exploration mode, turns away from side obstacles, uses a brief backward pulse only after front obstacles, and returns to forward exploration immediately on path_clear. Action states self-loop on path_clear so intended open-loop pulses are not preempted, while obstacle events force safe recovery.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate uncontrollable perception from controllable motion capability",
    "Use one-shot recovery states after obstacle events and return to clear exploration as soon as path_clear occurs",
    "Bias clear-space behavior toward move_forward, with random_walk only as an occasional alternate clear exploration action",
    "Use directed turns for side obstacles and brief backward escape only for front-obstacle recovery"
  ],
